# Cloudflare Pages custom headers.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Vite copies everything under public/ verbatim into dist/, so this file
# ships to dist/_headers and Cloudflare Pages picks it up automatically on
# deploy — no build-step wiring required.
#
# Issue #1300: front/admin-dashboard had zero security headers at all
# (it's a static SPA served via Cloudflare Pages, so there's no Vite/Node
# server config to attach them to). This adds the same baseline security
# headers front/web already has via next.config.ts/vercel.json, plus a
# Content-Security-Policy.
#
# #4804 : la CSP est désormais ENFORCÉE (plus de report-only). La politique
# liste explicitement toutes les origines chargées par le dashboard (API
# Render, WebSocket, Google Fonts, ui-avatars, tuiles OpenStreetMap).
#
# #7695 : la valeur de la CSP est GÉNÉRÉE AU BUILD (plugin `csp-headers` de
# vite.config.js, module scripts/csp.mjs) — ce fichier ne porte qu'un
# placeholder, remplacé dans dist/_headers. Deux durcissements :
#  - script-src perd 'unsafe-inline' (le bundle Vite n'émet que des scripts
#    externes, index.html n'a aucun script inline) ;
#  - connect-src perd le wildcard `https:`/`wss:` nu : les origines backend
#    sont dérivées de VITE_API_URL / VITE_WEBSOCKET_URL, connues au build
#    (deploy-admin-dashboard.yml les fournit). Un backend tenant-configuré
#    hors de ces variables exige donc un rebuild — c'est voulu : le wildcard
#    permettait d'exfiltrer vers n'importe quelle origine HTTPS.
# Test de garde : scripts/check-csp-guard.mjs (chaîné à `npm run build`)
# échoue si la CSP du build contient encore 'unsafe-inline' (script-src) ou
# un scheme nu dans connect-src.
#
# `upgrade-insecure-requests` was removed from the policy: Chrome logs
# « The Content Security Policy directive 'upgrade-insecure-requests' is
# ignored when delivered in a report-only policy. » as a console *error*,
# which the E2E smoke (error-handling.spec.js) treats as a failure. The
# directive is a no-op in report-only mode anyway — it only makes sense in
# an enforced policy, where it would be re-added deliberately.
#
# Origins referenced below come from what the admin dashboard actually
# loads/calls today:
#  - connect-src: VITE_API_URL (REST) and VITE_WEBSOCKET_URL (Socket.IO
#    realtime notifications, see src/stores/realtime.js), explicit origins
#    injected at build time (#7695).
#  - img-src: ui-avatars.com (generated user avatars) and OpenStreetMap tile
#    servers (Leaflet fleet map, src/views/fleet/FleetView.vue).
#  - style-src/font-src: Google Fonts (Inter, loaded via <link> in
#    index.html).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Content-Security-Policy: __CSP_BUILD_PLACEHOLDER__
